    "updated_at": "2025-08-28T23:48:41Z",
    "body": "Didn't get time to review your changes yet, but just to note about \"The treatment of the bitmap of the canvas and the bitmap of the rendering context and the bitmap of 2D rendering contexts, could be cleaned up\", @graveljp did a lot of work in that area in https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/9537, while also integrating the idea of a \"current output bitmap\".   \r\nMaybe we could extract what matches the current state (i.e. current output bitmap is always the top layer bitmap) from there in an editorial cleanup without having to wait on the layers to be done? @annevk is there a general rule for this kind of situation?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
